<p>In 2004, I began my journey in programming with the goal of solving internal challenges in the Logistics department at Unisul Virtual.
    Over time, I expanded my work to include the development of smaller-scale systems and the creation of reports for different areas within Unisul Virtual.</p>

<p>In 2009, Classroom Informática gave me the opportunity to work with Adobe Flex, even though during the interview I mentioned that I had only built two screens with it.
    I played an active role in the Flex community, maintained a blog, gave numerous talks, and trained more than 1,000 people.</p>

<p>After the end of Adobe Flex, I turned my focus exclusively to Videos and Moodle. In December 2017, I co-founded VideoFront, creating dozens of solutions to help the company expand its portfolio.
    We reached our peak in 2020 with the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/krausead/posts/pfbid0yPEJvDv6CMYWUkfSEiFf6W4dUXgoL8zNzFDJYbjGwK8VNHA3CRQ4LyvfqQt9gia5l" target="_blank">Most Digital Company 2020 – Micro Business Category</a> award, and again in <a href="https://www.facebook.com/krausead/posts/pfbid0hY8ndyercqQUscvJqvPxsNnNtFAcRYYq2xvYGzzVoEHp252Lk1DrvTaJj6WcrC8Pl" target="_blank">The Best of the Year 2022</a> in Foz do Iguaçu.</p>
